{"name":"Flame Lily","hex":"#ce0644","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flame lily","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Gloriosa lily (superb lily) whose yellow and red petals look like wavy, rising wisps of flame.","Synonym of wood lily."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flame_lily"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flame lily","blocks":[{"text":"Flame lily is a common name for several plants and may refer to:"},{"items":["Gloriosa superba","Lilium philadelphicum"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flame_lily","wikidata":"Q126008492"},{"title":"Gloriosa (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Gloriosa is a genus of 12 species in the plant family Colchicaceae, and includes the formerly recognised genus Littonia. They are native in tropical and southern Africa to Asia, and naturalised in Australia and the Pacific as well as being widely cultivated. The most common English names are flame lily, fire lily, gloriosa lily, glory lily, superb lily, climbing lily, and creeping lily."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Gloriosa_rothschildiana_01.jpg/330px-Gloriosa_rothschildiana_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gloriosa_(plant)","wikidata":"Q1454851"},{"title":"Flame","blocks":[{"text":"A flame is the visible, gaseous part of a fire. It is caused by a highly exothermic chemical reaction made in a thin zone. When flames are hot enough to have ionized gaseous components of sufficient density, they are then considered plasma."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/DancingFlames.jpg/330px-DancingFlames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flame","wikidata":"Q235544"},{"title":"Lilium","blocks":[{"text":"Lilium is a genus of herbaceous flowering plants growing from bulbs, all with large and often prominent flowers. Lilies are a group 